{"name":"Basswood","hex":"#c9b196","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"basswood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several trees of the genus Tilia; the lindens, especially Tilia americana, the American basswood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basswood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tilia americana","blocks":[{"text":"Tilia americana is a species of tree in the family Malvaceae. It is native to eastern North America, from southeast Manitoba east to New Brunswick, southwest to northeast Oklahoma, southeast to South Carolina, and west along the Niobrara River to Cherry County, Nebraska. It is the sole representative of its genus in the Western Hemisphere, assuming T. caroliniana is treated as a subspecies or local ecotype of T. americana. Common names include American basswood and American linden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tilia_americana_%28American_Linden%29_%2828268263222%29.jpg/330px-Tilia_americana_%28American_Linden%29_%2828268263222%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tilia_americana"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG/500px-Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG/1280px-Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG/500px-Tilia_americana%2C_Arnold_Arboretum_-_IMG_5911.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A specimen in the Arnold Arboretum leafing out in spring","link":"https